Result:
All ten findings posted as inline comments on PR #2525 (head `213957a3`). Review scope: the six branch commits (`ea47f457`…`213957a3`) — `GET /api/v1/search` + `search_service`, the `CommandPalette` component, tests, docs and the regenerated client.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/search_service.py",
    "line": 174,
    "summary": "The runs group runs a COUNT(*) and a page over `runs JOIN suites` filtered by `suite.name ILIKE … OR cast(run.id) LIKE …` on every keystroke — the OR on a cast defeats every index on `runs`, so an admin (include_all → `true`) pays a sequential scan of the whole runs table twice per debounce tick.",
    "failure_scenario": "100k+ runs (the #1986 scale), admin types `ab`/`abc`/`abcd`: each tick issues a count and a page both seq-scanning runs; p95 goes to seconds, one full-table scan per keystroke per user. Cheaper: resolve matching suite ids first and filter `Run.suite_id IN (...)` (hits `ix_runs_suite_created`), union the id-prefix branch separately, derive `truncated` from `limit + 1` rows instead of COUNT."
  },
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/CommandPalette.tsx",
    "line": 155,
    "summary": "`choose()` closes the palette, which schedules focus back to the OPENER (header Search button / whatever had focus before ⌘K), then navigates — after Enter a keyboard/screen-reader user lands on the header button of the new page (or `<body>` if the opener unmounted), never on the destination.",
    "failure_scenario": "⌘K, type `Orders`, Enter → URL is /suites/<id> but activeElement is the header Search button (the `isConnected` check runs synchronously before `navigate`). No route-change focus manager exists (PageTitle only sets document.title); the Playwright spec asserts URL + dialog count, not focus. Close without restoring focus on choose; move focus to the destination heading/<main>; keep opener-restore for Escape."
  },
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/CommandPalette.tsx",
    "line": 319,
    "summary": "Truncation is shown only as a `role=\"presentation\"` text node INSIDE the listbox, and the live status says `N results` — assistive tech never hears that a group has more matches, the one honesty signal the backend did a real COUNT to provide.",
    "failure_scenario": "30 checks match; sighted users see 'More checks match', but non-option descendants of a listbox are not exposed and `statusText` says `16 results.` A screen-reader user concludes the 16 are everything. Add truncated groups to `statusText` and move the hint out of the listbox."
  },
  {
    "file": "backend/app/services/search_service.py",
    "line": 208,
    "summary": "`_looks_like_uuid_prefix` accepts any 4+ char hex/hyphen string, so ordinary words and numbers (`cafe`, `face`, `dead`, `beef`, `2024`, `1234`, `----`) are treated as run-id prefixes and pull in unrelated runs with no cue why they matched.",
    "failure_scenario": "Search `cafe` for suite 'Cafe sales': with 100k v4 UUIDs ~1–2 random runs of other suites appear in the Runs group under their own suite names, and the query takes the index-defeating `CAST(id) LIKE` path. Require ≥ 8 hex chars (first UUID group) and mark id-matched runs in the sublabel."
  },
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/CommandPalette.tsx",
    "line": 104,
    "summary": "The window-level ⌘K/Ctrl+K handler fires regardless of focus context or whether the event was already consumed — inside Monaco (⌘K is its chord prefix), inside other open dialogs, and on auto-repeat.",
    "failure_scenario": "Author presses ⌘K ⌘C in the custom-SQL editor: Monaco enters chord-wait and the palette opens over it; the ⌘C goes to the palette input. With a delete-confirm open, ⌘K stacks the palette above it. Skip when `event.defaultPrevented`, `event.repeat`, or target is inside `.monaco-editor` / another `[role=dialog]`."
  },
